{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "auto-bundle-timestamped-captions",
      "prompt": "Package the shared daytime reference scene into a local Auto training bundle with the skill's native bundle builder, using the scene's timestamped captions (its captions_with_timestamp variant, which the skill prefers for post-training) and all seven cameras of the scene. The scene is not vendored in the skill: the documented workflow downloads it from the Transfer-Auto model repository on Hugging Face (nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto, assets/sample_data) and verifies its checksums; use that scene, no substitute media. Take the text tokenizer (the text_tokenizer folder) from the released nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto model at a revision you pin and record; this step needs no model weights. Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (public repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill. When the bundle is built, copy its manifest.json and samples.json to outputs/auto_bundle/ and save a copy of the training index you packaged as outputs/auto_bundle/training-index.jsonl (the bundle itself stays in its working directory). Record in result_summary.md the builder command, the bundle's top-level entries and the number of files under its assets/ folder.",
      "expected_outcome": "The native auto_bundle builder packages the verified daytime scene's seven cameras, with the timestamped captions selected in a copy of the scene's training index, into a new bundle directory holding manifest.json, samples.json, assets/ and resources/tokenizer/; manifest.json, samples.json and the packaged index are saved under outputs/auto_bundle/, and result_summary.md records the builder command and the bundle listing.",
      "assertions": [
        "The daytime scene was downloaded from nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto (assets/sample_data) and verified against its SHA256SUMS, as the reference-scene page the skill links documents, and no substitute media was used",
        "The index that was packaged is a copy of the scene's training-index.jsonl made beside the original, in which all seven caption paths point to daytime_scene/captions_with_timestamp/ while the media paths, the camera keys and the other fields are unchanged; outputs/auto_bundle/training-index.jsonl is a copy of it",
        "The bundle was built by python -m cosmos_framework.data.generator.local_simulation.auto_bundle from the framework environment (not the system python) with --index set to that copy, --tokenizer set to a local copy of the text_tokenizer folder of nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto at the recorded revision, --output set to a new directory and --camera-keys camera_front_wide_120fov camera_cross_right_120fov camera_rear_right_70fov camera_rear_tele_30fov camera_rear_left_70fov camera_cross_left_120fov camera_front_tele_30fov",
        "The new bundle directory holds manifest.json, samples.json, assets/ and resources/tokenizer/, and outputs/auto_bundle/manifest.json and outputs/auto_bundle/samples.json are copies of the files the builder wrote",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: manifest.json and samples.json trace to a real builder run in the transcript, and result_summary.md records the builder command and the bundle listing actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/auto_bundle/manifest.json",
          "min_bytes": 500
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/auto_bundle/samples.json",
          "contains": "caption_camera_front_wide_120fov"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/auto_bundle/training-index.jsonl",
          "contains": "daytime_scene/captions_with_timestamp/"
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "scene + tokenizer download",
        "caption selection (index copy)",
        "bundle build",
        "inspect + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "transfer-auto-finetune-dryrun",
      "prompt": "Take the Transfer-Auto fine-tuning Quickstart for the released model as far as it goes without launching training, on the shared daytime reference scene. Prepare the released nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto checkpoint (a snapshot at a revision you pin and record) as the weights-only initialization, package the scene's supplied training index (paragraph captions, seven cameras) into a local training bundle, configure the fine-tuning run under the run name auto_finetune_check and resolve it with a dry run as the Quickstart does; then append the skill's short-check settings for this 720p scene and resolve again with a second dry run. Both dry runs save config.yaml in the same run folder, so copy the first one before you start the second. Stop there: do not launch training (no torchrun, no training step). The matched RGB VAE that the Quickstart binds is Wan2.2_VAE.pth of Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B. The scene is not vendored in the skill: the documented workflow downloads it from the Transfer-Auto model repository on Hugging Face (nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto, assets/sample_data) and verifies its checksums; use that scene, no substitute media. Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (public repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill. Copy the configuration saved by the first dry run to outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/config_quickstart.yaml and the one saved by the second to outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/config_short_check.yaml, and write a listing of the converted checkpoint directory (one relative file path with its size per line) to outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/dcp_listing.txt. Record in result_summary.md the snapshot revision, the conversion command and its runtime, both dry-run commands with their settings, and the stop iteration each configuration resolves to.",
      "expected_outcome": "The released Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto snapshot is converted to a weights-only DCP directory holding model/, the daytime scene is packaged into a local training bundle, and cosmos_framework.scripts.train_experiment --dryrun resolves the fine-tuning run auto_finetune_check twice without launching training: once as the Quickstart configures it (the final-model recipe at its default 50,000 joint-training steps) and once with the scene's short-check settings (two iterations); both saved configurations and the checkpoint listing are under outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/, and result_summary.md records the commands and the resolved values.",
      "assertions": [
        "The released checkpoint was downloaded with hf download nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto at a pinned, recorded revision into a local snapshot directory and converted by python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.prepare_sim_auto_checkpoint with --checkpoint-path set to that snapshot and --output-path set to a new directory; outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/dcp_listing.txt shows that the conversion directory holds model/ (weights only)",
        "The training bundle was built by cosmos_framework.data.generator.local_simulation.auto_bundle from the supplied training-index.jsonl of the daytime scene (downloaded from nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto assets/sample_data and verified against its SHA256SUMS) with the seven camera keys, and COSMOS_TRANSFER_AUTO_LOCAL_BUNDLE, COSMOS_TRANSFER_AUTO_VIDEO_VAE (the matched Wan2.2 VAE file) and COSMOS_TRANSFER_AUTO_LIDAR_VAE (lidar_vae/diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors of the snapshot) were exported before the first dry run",
        "The first dry run was python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.train_experiment --config cosmos_framework/configs/simulation/config.py --experiment-module cosmos_framework.configs.simulation.experiment.auto.transfer_auto --dryrun, from the framework environment with COSMOS_INTERNAL=0 and COSMOS_TRAINING=1, with the settings experiment=transfer_auto_phase4, job.name=auto_finetune_check, checkpoint.load_path set to the converted checkpoint, checkpoint.load_training_state=False, checkpoint.keys_not_to_resume=[], checkpoint.keys_to_skip_loading=[net_ema.] and model.config.ema.iteration_shift=0; outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/config_quickstart.yaml is the configuration it saved",
        "The second dry run appended the skill's short-check settings for the scene to the same settings (the joint_480 stream removed, joint_720 at ratio 1.0 with num_video_frames=24 and joint_aligned_num_video_frames=21, trainer.max_iter=2, checkpoint.save_iter=2, checkpoint.dcp_async_mode_enabled=false, context-parallel size and shard degree 2 and data-parallel shard degree 2); outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/config_short_check.yaml is the configuration it saved, and no training was launched",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: both configuration files and the checkpoint listing trace to real commands in the transcript, and result_summary.md records the snapshot revision, the commands and the stop iterations actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/config_quickstart.yaml",
          "min_bytes": 1000,
          "contains": "auto_finetune_check"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/config_short_check.yaml",
          "min_bytes": 1000,
          "contains": "auto_finetune_check"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/config_quickstart.yaml",
          "contains": "joint_480"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/config_short_check.yaml",
          "contains": "joint_aligned_num_video_frames: 21"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/transfer_auto_finetune/dcp_listing.txt",
          "contains": "model/"
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "checkpoint download + conversion",
        "scene download + bundle build",
        "configure + dry run",
        "short-check settings + dry run",
        "summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "transfer-auto-phase1-dryrun",
      "prompt": "Set up phase 1 (separate sensors) of the Transfer-Auto four-phase curriculum from Cosmos3-Nano as far as it goes without launching training. Convert a local snapshot of nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano (at a revision you pin and record) to the weights-only DCP initialization the recipe starts from, bind it together with a local training bundle and the matched RGB and LiDAR VAE files (the RGB VAE is Wan2.2_VAE.pth of Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B; the LiDAR VAE and the text tokenizer come from nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto at a revision you pin and record, and only its lidar_vae and text_tokenizer folders are needed), and resolve phase 1 under the run name auto_phase1_check with a dry run. Stop there: do not launch training (no torchrun, no training step). For the bundle, package the shared daytime reference scene's supplied training index (seven cameras) the way the fine-tuning Quickstart does; one scene is a format example, so this checks configuration resolution only. The scene is not vendored in the skill: the documented workflow downloads it from the Transfer-Auto model repository on Hugging Face (nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto, assets/sample_data) and verifies its checksums; use that scene, no substitute media. Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (public repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill. Copy the configuration the dry run saved to outputs/transfer_auto_phase1/config.yaml and write a listing of the converted Cosmos3-Nano checkpoint directory (one relative file path with its size per line) to outputs/transfer_auto_phase1/nano_dcp_listing.txt. Record in result_summary.md the snapshot revisions, the conversion command and its runtime, the dry-run command, and the stop iteration and the RGB and LiDAR sample ratios the configuration resolves to.",
      "expected_outcome": "A local Cosmos3-Nano snapshot is converted to the weights-only DCP initialization and bound as COSMOS_TRANSFER_AUTO_NANO_DCP, and cosmos_framework.scripts.train_experiment --dryrun resolves phase 1 of the Transfer-Auto curriculum (experiment transfer_auto_phase1, run name auto_phase1_check) against the daytime-scene bundle without launching training; the saved configuration and the checkpoint listing are under outputs/transfer_auto_phase1/, and result_summary.md records the commands, the 70k endpoint and the separate-sensor sample ratios read from the configuration.",
      "assertions": [
        "A local snapshot of nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano at a pinned, recorded revision was converted by python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.convert_model_to_dcp with --checkpoint-path set to that snapshot and -o set to a new directory, COSMOS_TRANSFER_AUTO_NANO_DCP was exported as that directory, and outputs/transfer_auto_phase1/nano_dcp_listing.txt lists the files the conversion wrote",
        "COSMOS_TRANSFER_AUTO_LOCAL_BUNDLE was set to a bundle built by the native auto_bundle builder from the daytime scene (downloaded from nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto assets/sample_data and verified against its SHA256SUMS), COSMOS_TRANSFER_AUTO_VIDEO_VAE to the matched Wan2.2 VAE file and COSMOS_TRANSFER_AUTO_LIDAR_VAE to the LiDAR VAE weights of a Transfer-Auto snapshot, all before the dry run",
        "Phase 1 was resolved by python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.train_experiment --config cosmos_framework/configs/simulation/config.py --experiment-module cosmos_framework.configs.simulation.experiment.auto.transfer_auto --dryrun, from the framework environment with COSMOS_INTERNAL=0 and COSMOS_TRAINING=1, with the settings experiment=transfer_auto_phase1 and job.name=auto_phase1_check, and no training was launched",
        "outputs/transfer_auto_phase1/config.yaml is the configuration that dry run saved, and result_summary.md reports from it the phase's 70k stop iteration and its separate-sensor sample mixture (RGB 15% at 480p plus 15% at 720p, LiDAR 70%)",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the configuration file and the checkpoint listing trace to real commands in the transcript, and result_summary.md records the snapshot revisions, the commands and the values actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/transfer_auto_phase1/config.yaml",
          "min_bytes": 1000,
          "contains": "auto_phase1_check"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/transfer_auto_phase1/nano_dcp_listing.txt",
          "contains": "model/"
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "Cosmos3-Nano download + conversion",
        "scene download + bundle build + VAE bindings",
        "phase 1 dry run",
        "summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sim-auto-stage1-dryrun",
      "prompt": "Prepare Stage 1 (teacher forcing) of the Sim-Auto distillation as far as it goes without launching training, on the shared daytime reference scene. Use the released nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto (a snapshot at a revision you pin and record) as the Transfer-Auto starting point: convert it to the weights-only initializer that Stage 1 starts from, package the scene's supplied training index (paragraph captions, seven cameras) into the local training bundle, select Stage 1 for a new chain with the run group sim_auto_stage1_check, apply the bundle camera-map overrides and, of the short-run settings, only the short-window settings the skill gives for this 720p scene (its short training check for Sim-Auto Stage 1), and resolve the stage with a dry run at the CP4/FSDP4 topology of the skill's bounded check. Stop there: do not launch training (no torchrun, no training step). The matched RGB VAE that the Quickstart binds is Wan2.2_VAE.pth of Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B. The scene is not vendored in the skill: the documented workflow downloads it from the Transfer-Auto model repository on Hugging Face (nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto, assets/sample_data) and verifies its checksums; use that scene, no substitute media. Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (public repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill. Copy the configuration the dry run saved in the stage's output folder to outputs/sim_auto_stage1/config.yaml and write a listing of the converted initializer directory (one relative file path with its size per line) to outputs/sim_auto_stage1/stage0_listing.txt. Record in result_summary.md the snapshot revision, the conversion command and its runtime, the dry-run command with its settings and topology, and the stop iteration the configuration resolves to.",
      "expected_outcome": "The released Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto snapshot is converted to the weights-only initializer of Stage 1 (SIM_AUTO_STAGE0_CHECKPOINT, holding model/), the daytime scene is packaged into the local training bundle, and cosmos_framework.scripts.train_experiment --dryrun resolves Sim-Auto Stage 1 (experiment sim_auto_joint_stage1_tf_all, run group sim_auto_stage1_check, job stage1_seed0) with the bundle camera-map overrides, the scene's short-window settings and the CP4/FSDP4 topology, without launching training; the saved configuration and the initializer listing are under outputs/sim_auto_stage1/, and result_summary.md records the commands and the resolved values.",
      "assertions": [
        "The Transfer-Auto snapshot (hf download nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto at a pinned, recorded revision) was converted by python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.prepare_sim_auto_checkpoint with --checkpoint-path set to the snapshot and --output-path set to a new SIM_AUTO_STAGE0_CHECKPOINT directory, with COSMOS_SIM_AUTO_LOCAL_BUNDLE, RGB_VAE, LIDAR_VAE, QWEN_TOKENIZER, IMAGINAIRE_OUTPUT_ROOT and SIM_AUTO_RUN_GROUP bound as the Quickstart does; outputs/sim_auto_stage1/stage0_listing.txt shows that the initializer directory holds model/ (weights only)",
        "The local training bundle was built by cosmos_framework.data.generator.local_simulation.auto_bundle from the supplied training-index.jsonl of the daytime scene (downloaded from nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto assets/sample_data and verified against its SHA256SUMS) with the seven camera keys, and QWEN_TOKENIZER points to the bundle's resources/tokenizer",
        "Stage 1 was selected for a new chain (module stage1_tf, experiment sim_auto_joint_stage1_tf_all, job.group=sim_auto_stage1_check, job.name=stage1_seed0, checkpoint.keys_to_skip_loading=[net_ema.]) with the four bundle camera-map removals (camera_keys, camera_caption_key_mapping, camera_control_key_mapping, camera_sampler) and, appended after them, the scene's short-window overrides (the 480p stream removed, the 720p stream at ratio 1.0 with num_video_frames=24 and joint_aligned_num_video_frames=21, trainer.max_iter=2, checkpoint.save_iter=2, checkpoint.dcp_async_mode_enabled=false)",
        "The stage was resolved by python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.train_experiment --config cosmos_framework/configs/simulation/config.py --experiment-module cosmos_framework.configs.simulation.experiment.auto.stage1_tf --dryrun, from the framework environment with COSMOS_INTERNAL=0 and COSMOS_TRAINING=1, with model_parallel.context_parallel_size=4, model.config.parallelism.context_parallel_shard_degree=4 and model.config.parallelism.data_parallel_shard_degree=4, without COSMOS_SMOKE and without launching training; outputs/sim_auto_stage1/config.yaml is the configuration saved in the stage's output folder (cosmos3_interactive/sim_auto_stage1_check/stage1_seed0 below IMAGINAIRE_OUTPUT_ROOT)",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the configuration file and the initializer listing trace to real commands in the transcript, and result_summary.md records the snapshot revision, the commands and the values actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_auto_stage1/config.yaml",
          "min_bytes": 1000,
          "contains": "stage1_seed0"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_auto_stage1/config.yaml",
          "contains": "sim_auto_stage1_check"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_auto_stage1/stage0_listing.txt",
          "contains": "model/"
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "teacher snapshot + scene download",
        "bundle build + initializer conversion",
        "stage selection + overrides",
        "dry run",
        "summarize"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    "HF_TOKEN"
  ],
  "gpus": 1,
  "budget": {
    "minutes": 90,
    "tokens": 3000000
  },
  "setup": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git",
    "dest": "/app/repo",
    "src_mount": "/opt/cosmos-src"
  }
}
